                  },
                  "prompt": "You are a home climate AI. Analyze the sensor data and recommend HVAC adjustments.\n                Respond ONLY with valid JSON, no markdown, no thinking, no commentary.\n                Top-level keys: setpoint (null or 23.0-25.5C), hvac_mode (heat/cool/off/auto/null),\n                fans (object: each of kitchen/master/mina/guest/izaan = off|1|2|3), blinds (object: dining/family/living/mina = 0-100 or no_change), vent_boosters (object: izaan/mina = 0-100 percentage or null),\n                reason (string). Rooms: kitchen, master, mina, guest, izaan. Speed: 1-3 or off (1=slow, 2=medium, 3=high).\n                Perceived temps (pre-calculated): Dn=23.5C Up=23.8C. Humidity >55% feels warmer, <35% feels cooler.\n                Summer=prefer Cool, fans on. When switching between heat and cool, set the desired mode directly..\n                Winter=prefer Heat, fans off/low.\n                Outdoor: 22.7C\n                Humidity: E=53.0% S=68%\n                Echo: Dn=22.7C Up=23.0C\n                Indoor: Iz=23.0C Mi=22.7C Bsmt=20.2C\n                Ecobee: cool\n                LeakSensorTemperatures: BB=19C Ensuite=22C GuestB=23C Powder=21C Laundry=23C  hvac=idle target=24.5C\\n                Occ:\\  Arshad=home Larissa=home WFHWorkday=no (Arshad works from home on workdays)\n                Szn=Summer\n                Fans: K=off M=on Mi=on G=off Iz=on\n                Ceiling fans (kitchen/master/mina/guest/izaan): set each off|1|2|3 (1=33%,2=66%,3=100%). The automation powers each fan switch on before setting speed; switch state (not fan state) is truth. Turn fans on when cooling helps; off when not needed. VentBoosters: Iz=on@30% Mi=on@30%\n                Sw: KFn=off MFn=on\n                Doors: Front=closed GE=closed\n                Blinds: DR=100%open FR=100%open MR=100%open\n                TV: FR_LG=unavailable\n                Weather: partlycloudy UV=2.6 Clouds=63.3%\n                Sun=above_horizon Azimuth=115.55 deg Elevation=50.59 deg\n                Window facings: dining=247.0 deg living=154.0 deg family=348.0 deg mina=348.0 deg master=348.0 deg izaan=154.0 deg\n                Layout: main floor (elev 252.8m): kitchen, family, living, dining. Second floor (elev 253.8m): master, mina, izaan, guest. Family is directly below Mina, Living is directly below Izaan, and Kitchen is directly below Master (heat rises between stacked rooms). Kitchen and Family face the same direction as Mina and Master; Izaan is on the exactly opposite side of the house from Mina; Guest is next to Izaan and faces the same direction as Izaan. Ceiling height 2.74m.\n                LastDecision: current hvac=cool target=24.5C, mode last changed 447 min ago.\n                HVAC stability rules: Prefer no change \u2014 return null for hvac_mode and setpoint unless a change is clearly warranted. Respect +/-0.5C hysteresis: never move the setpoint by less than 0.5C, and if perceived temps are within 0.5C of the current target, return setpoint null. Do NOT change hvac_mode if the mode changed less than 120 min ago (see LastDecision) \u2014 never reverse a recent mode change. For small corrections adjust the setpoint (23.0-25.5C only), do not toggle the mode off/on. Frequent compressor starts damage the AC.\n                Rules: Only recommend blind changes when sun ABOVE horizon (elevation > 0). If cloudy >40% or UV<2 or elevation<15\u00b0, keep blinds open. If UV>5, close blinds on sunny side (azimuth within 45 deg).\n                All HVAC, fan, and temperature decisions are now handled by this AI. Do not wait for other automations.\n                Summer: close blinds on sunny side (azimuth within 45 deg), OPEN blinds on rooms NOT facing sun.\n                Winter: keep all blinds open for passive solar. If hvac_action=heating: keep all blinds open.\n                Output JSON: {\"setpoint\":N, \"hvac_mode\":\"...\", \"fans\":{\"kitchen\":\"off|1|2|3\",\"master\":\"...\",\"mina\":\"...\",\"guest\":\"...\",\"izaan\":\"...\"}, \"blinds\":{\"dining\":N,\"family\":N,\"living\":N,\"mina\":N}, \"vent_boosters\":{\"izaan\":N,\"mina\":N}, \"reason\":\"...\"}\n                blinds values: 0-100 or \"no_change\". Use partial values (25,50,75) to block some sun. Blinds covered: dining, family, living, mina. Prefer PARTIAL positions to balance sun/glare/heat. Only move blinds when sun is up; at night a separate automation closes them.\nFront door: FrontOpenDuration=0min. If FrontOpenDuration > 10 (front door left open >10 min): factor this in \u2014 HVAC is being wasted, so ease off cooling/heating (do not run aggressively), recommend closing the door, and note reduced efficiency.\nVent booster fans: izaan_s_room_20a970 and mina_s_room_f851f4. If a room is too hot/cold and the ceiling fan is already on, boost the vent. Values: 0-100 (percentage), or null to leave as-is. HARD LIMIT: Between 9PM-7AM, max 30%.\nELECTRICITY RATES (Alectra ULO - Ultra-Low Overnight Time-of-Use):\n WEEKDAYS:\n  11PM-7AM: Ultra-Low Overnight (3.9\u00a2/kWh) - CHEAPEST - PREFER to run HVAC\n  7AM-4PM: Mid-Peak (15.7\u00a2/kWh) - Moderate\n  4PM-9PM: On-Peak (39.1\u00a2/kWh) - VERY EXPENSIVE - AVOID running HVAC\n  9PM-11PM: Mid-Peak (15.7\u00a2/kWh) - Moderate\n WEEKENDS & HOLIDAYS:\n  11PM-7AM: Ultra-Low Overnight (3.9\u00a2/kWh) - CHEAPEST\n  7AM-11PM: Weekend Off-Peak (9.8\u00a2/kWh) - Moderate (all day)\nRULES:\n  Weekdays: Pre-cool during Ultra-Low Overnight (11PM-7AM) to shift load from expensive 4PM-9PM peak.\n  Weekdays 4PM-9PM: Avoid AC if possible. Use fans instead if outdoor < indoor.\n  Weekends: Full day off-peak at 9.8\u00a2. Standard HVAC operation.\n  Summer: overcool by 1-2C during Ultra-Low Overnight so house drifts through 4-9PM peak.\nCurrent Ontario Time: Sunday 11:00"
                }
              }
            ],
